      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِجَاعٌ</span></b>  The <i>nose-rein of a camel:</i> (IDrd, K:)
or the <i>part thereof which falls upon the nose of
the camel:</i> pl. [of pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْجِعَةٌ</span> and [of mult.]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُجُعٌ</span>: (K:) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجَعَ</span> in the phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجَعَ فُلَانٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى أَنْفِ بَعِيرِهِ</span> [q. v.]. (IDrd.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  It is also an
inf. n.: see 1, in the middle of the paragraph.

